%% P02 lifecycle of the CHILD process for one run (Linux). Arrow labels name the event that causes each transition.
stateDiagram-v2
    direction LR
    [*] --> New: parent calls Popen(...)<br/>(observed - vfork + execve)
    New --> Ready: created and admitted<br/>(PID 525 assigned)
    Ready --> Running: scheduler dispatch
    Running --> Ready: preempted by timer<br/>(possible - not observed)
    Running --> Blocked: input() - read(0) finds no line<br/>(ps S+ / wchan wait_woken)
    Blocked --> Ready: Enter pressed - terminal input arrives
    Running --> Exited: return EXIT_CODE (7)<br/>exit_group(7)
    Exited --> Reaped: parent wait() / wait4 collects status 7
    Reaped --> [*]

    note right of Running
        First Running period = 0.75 s CPU phase
        (utime 75 ticks @ 100 Hz).
        After Enter: write file, print, exit.
    end note
    note left of Exited
        Exited but not yet reaped = POSIX zombie (Z).
        Observed separately in extra-zombie-reaping.txt
    end note
